WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:07.390
In 2024, Americans bought about 3.30 trillion
dollars of goods from other countries.

2
00:00:07.390 --> 00:00:12.390
They sold only about 2.08 trillion
dollars of goods in return.

3
00:00:12.390 --> 00:00:14.300
Services helped a little.

4
00:00:14.300 --> 00:00:19.050
But the current account deficit
still hit 1.13 trillion dollars,

5
00:00:19.050 --> 00:00:22.150
3.9 percent of GDP.

6
00:00:22.150 --> 00:00:25.270
So when a country buys more
from the world than it sells,

7
00:00:25.270 --> 00:00:27.400
how does it pay the difference?

8
00:00:27.400 --> 00:00:31.350
In this mission, you'll calculate
a current account from net exports,

9
00:00:31.350 --> 00:00:35.490
net income from abroad, and
net unilateral transfers.

10
00:00:35.490 --> 00:00:38.960
Then you'll see why every
transaction is recorded twice,

11
00:00:38.960 --> 00:00:41.430
and what the second entry tells you.

12
00:00:41.430 --> 00:00:44.490
Your mission: find out
how a country covers what

13
00:00:44.490 --> 00:00:46.450
it cannot pay from its earnings.
